1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,880
O sunar za no to rai za auga.

2
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,150
Whoa.

3
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,800
Everything looks way brighter now.

4
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:16,060
So this is night vision magic.

5
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:19,317
I guess spriggans are good
for something after all.

6
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,224
I don't know if that was
a compliment or a diss.

7
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:24,737
You're practicing the magic you can use.

8
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:25,877
That's the important thing.

9
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,717
And projecting illusions
is one of your specialties.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:29,630
Illusions?

11
00:00:29,713 --> 00:00:30,968
Yeah, to trick people with.

12
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:34,177
It's cool, but it's not gonna
help anyone much in combat.

13
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:37,197
But you never know in a
life-or-death situation

14
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,456
your lame spriggan magic
might actually come in handy.

15
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,480
Now that was a diss.

16
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,117
I'll

17
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,340
I'll go over it.

18
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,061
I'll go over it.

19
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:09,120
I'll go over it.

20
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,877
Them with the effects of the magic
that's how you memorize spells.

21
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:34,157
I never thought I'd be in a game.

22
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,517
And have to memorize words
from a different language.

23
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:41,597
Oh and just so you know the higher
ranked spells have about 20 words.

24
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,510
Holy crap.

25
00:02:42,593 --> 00:02:44,017
I'll just stick to fighting.

26
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,077
Then would you quit complaining?

27
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:49,117
Oh someone's messaging me.

28
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:50,917
Sorry I have to get this.

29
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,817
Sure it's reckon again.

30
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:54,817
It's.

31
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:57,253
Probably nothing, but I'll check anyway.

32
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:00,880
It says, I was right, be careful, S.

33
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,060
That's it.

34
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:04,380
What's that mean? S?

35
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:07,300
Sa-shi-su-oh.

36
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:08,890
What's wrong?

37
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,080
Oh, nothing.

38
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:13,017
Daddy, I'm picking up movement behind us.

39
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:14,159
Are they monsters?

40
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:17,100
Uh-uh, they're players. A lot.

41
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:19,420
12 total. You're kidding.

42
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:23,197
Oh, I've got a bad feeling about this.

43
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,840
We better take cover.

44
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,500
Okay, but where?

45
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,030
Ha!

46
00:03:28,113 --> 00:03:29,587
Just leave everything to me.

47
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,780
Hey, easy.

48
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,640
She shall always groan lobuto.

49
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,180
We can talk, but we have to
be really quiet about it.

50
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:48,577
Anything louder than a whisper
and it's gonna break the spell.

51
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:49,490
Okay.

52
00:03:49,573 --> 00:03:51,501
They'll be coming into view soon.

53
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,840
What is that? You see it?

54
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:59,320
No, I can't see anything.

55
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,357
I can tell it's not a player.

56
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:02,620
It's got red eyes.

57
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:03,980
Kind of like a bat.

58
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:16,169
Why'd you break our cover?

59
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:19,477
Because that thing out there is
a high-level tracing searcher.

60
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,854
We have to destroy it!

61
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:31,060
Come on, we gotta go!

62
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,417
Can't we just hide behind
one of your spells again?

63
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,206
They already know we're here.

64
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:37,857
That tracer had us pegged.

65
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:39,817
Hiding's not gonna do us any good.

66
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:42,780
Besides, that bat was a
fire element familiar.

67
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:45,637
That can only mean the ones
who are tracking us are...

68
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,860
The salamanders.

69
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:53,457
What's a party of salamanders
doing way down here?

70
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:54,397
Whoa!

71
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,598
Check out the lake.

72
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,437
Looks like we're gonna get away!

73
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:06,049
Watch where you're
going or you'll fall in!

74
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,640
That won't work.

75
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,837
Why didn't you tell me that before?

76
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:24,744
Oh, right, like it's my
fault you're in a hurry.

77
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,547
It's an earth magic barrier.

78
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:29,097
You can bash on it all day
and it won't destroy it.

79
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:31,237
Can we jump in the lake
and swim around it?

80
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:32,150
Nope.

81
00:05:32,233 --> 00:05:34,277
At least, not unless you want to be lunch.

82
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,897
The water is filled with
high-level monsters.

83
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:40,980
The Undines are the only ones who
can take those kinds of things on.

84
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,986
Then I guess the only
option left is to fight.

85
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:47,655
I'm not going to argue with
that, but it won't be easy.

86
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:51,597
If the Salamanders have high-level
earth magic, it can only mean one thing.

87
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:54,033
They have a powerful mage on their side.

88
00:05:56,580 --> 00:06:00,497
Leafa, I know you're good with the
sword, so don't take this the wrong way.

89
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:02,992
But could you back me up from here on in?

90
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:06,920
I need you to stay behind
and focus on healing me.

91
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:10,276
That way I can fight harder
and not worry about my HP.

92
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:36,760
They're targeting him
with everything they got!

93
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,900
Lisa Park!

94
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:43,040
Rando Doroto!

95
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:51,660
Lisa! Soap!

96
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:02,920
Su-fi-la-he-do-as-ta-lu-proto-supal-bani!

97
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,010
Uh-oh.

98
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,720
What do we do?

99
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,374
He's gonna run out of HP at some point.

100
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,240
That's enough, Kirito!

101
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:36,657
If we lose, it'll just mean a
couple extra hours of flying!

102
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:38,328
Let's give up while we can!

103
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,310
No way.

104
00:07:41,393 --> 00:07:45,066
As long as I'm alive, I'm not
gonna let anyone in my party die.

105
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,300
I won't let that happen again.

106
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,840
What the hell? What's he doing?

107
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,190
Hurry!

108
00:08:09,273 --> 00:08:10,437
This is your only chance!

109
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,517
What do you mean?

110
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,737
You have to use all the Main you have!

111
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:17,317
Hurry and focus on shielding
him from the next magic attack!

112
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,230
Uh, okay.

113
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,480
But I don't think it's gonna help.

114
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:24,717
Deku, Baupa, Eugene,

115
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:28,460
Rando, Musti, Kara, Ressa!

116
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:36,900
Su, Shalu, Lindo, Ashnia, Batu, Emi, Ogu!

117
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:40,220
Mama, Sepa! Speldo!

118
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,680
Rando, Doroto!

119
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,980
Do it now, Daddy!

120
00:08:57,420 --> 00:08:59,140
He's using illusion magic.

121
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:03,664
But all that's going to do is make
him look like a giant monster.

122
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,620
Is that...Kirito?

123
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,490
Idiots!

124
00:09:39,573 --> 00:09:40,677
Don't break formation!

125
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,590
It's not real!

126
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:42,637
Don't be afraid!

127
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:46,485
He can't hurt us if you stick to
the plan and stay in formation!

128
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,000
Hit him with an explosion spell!

129
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:04,060
You fava!

130
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,920
Eihon!

131
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:17,020
No!

132
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:18,810
No!

133
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,280
Retreat! Retreat!

134
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:32,560
Retreat!

135
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:01,800
Wait, Kittito!

136
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:03,660
Hold on, don't kill him!

137
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,880
Isn't my daddy amazing?

138
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:16,713
Okay, if you want to live you better
tell me who sent you asshats after us

139
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:20,297
Never kill me if you want you've got it.

140
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:21,320
Oh, man.

141
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:22,920
Now that was cool

142
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:29,320
That was an awesome fight, huh?

143
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:32,597
Your plan wasn't shabby
either if I was alone I

144
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,837
wouldn't have lasted a
minute against you dorks.

145
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:36,677
What are you telling him that for?

146
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:38,840
Let me handle this Listen up.

147
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:41,237
I want to see if you
and me can make a deal.

148
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,150
Check it out.

149
00:11:42,233 --> 00:11:45,277
Those are all the items in Yul'd
I want after beating your asses.

150
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:48,657
All you have to do is answer my
questions and they could be yours.

151
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:49,570
Sound good?

152
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:53,470
Seriously?

153
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:54,830
Totally.

154
00:11:59,040 --> 00:11:59,870
Oh, men.

155
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,675
It's like they forgot we're even here.

156
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:07,717
Earlier this evening, I got
an urgent text from Jitakasu.

157
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:11,017
He's the leader of the mage
squad, or, well, he used to be.

158
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:14,137
Anyway, I got this text telling
us all to meet him here.

159
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:18,457
And when I showed up, he said he needed
12 of us to go on a hunt for two players.

160
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,952
At first, I thought it was overkill, but,

161
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:24,700
well, he said you guys took
out Kagemune, so it made sense.

162
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,520
Who's this Kagemune guy?

163
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:30,437
He's the leader of the lancer squad,
and he's known for hunting sylphs.

164
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:34,049
But yesterday, he got creamed
in a fight and had to retreat.

165
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,206
That was you guys, wasn't it?

166
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:41,537
Wait, why is Jitakasu so interested
in getting us out of the way?

167
00:12:41,620 --> 00:12:43,267
The order came from the top.

168
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:47,920
Something about you interfering
with the plan. Yeah? What plan?

169
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,780
Hey, hey, I'm just a grunt.

170
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:51,137
They don't tell me anything.

171
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:54,357
But I'm pretty sure something
really big's about to go down.

172
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,793
When I logged on today,

173
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:59,860
I saw this big-ass swarm of
salamander troops heading up north.

174
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:01,750
No way.

175
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:03,997
They're gonna go try to clear
the world tree, aren't they?

176
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,220
I doubt that.

177
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:07,237
Someone figured that to take the tree,

178
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:09,657
the whole army would need
ancient weapon-class equipment,

179
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:11,564
and we can't afford that stuff.

180
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,578
That's everything I know, I promise.

181
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:19,095
You weren't lying about your
end of the deal, were you?

182
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,030
No.

183
00:13:20,113 --> 00:13:21,440
I'm a man of my word, partner.

184
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:24,290
Hey,

185
00:13:24,373 --> 00:13:28,757
that big ugly monster that was tearing
everything up, was that you or an illusion?

186
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,580
Yeah, I don't remember.

187
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:32,175
Wait, you don't know?

188
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:33,600
Not really.

189
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:35,117
It just happens sometimes.

190
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:38,737
In the heat of battle, I'll snap
and can't remember a thing after.

191
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:39,960
Whoa, scary.

192
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:43,257
I think I remember most of what
happened this last time, though.

193
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:46,700
Like, I know I used that spell
Yui suggested. Do it now!

194
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:49,040
I also remember getting huge.

195
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:50,280
That was cool.

196
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:54,640
I remember losing my sword
and then grabbing people.

197
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:57,697
And you were chomping down
on them, remember that?

198
00:13:57,780 --> 00:13:58,877
Oh, yeah.

199
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,937
I totally felt like a monster.

200
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:03,080
All eating people and everything.

201
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:05,940
So, uh, what did they taste like?

202
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:08,777
Kind of like grilled meat
just before it gets burnt.

203
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:09,857
All crispy and...

204
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:10,770
Okay, good.

205
00:14:10,853 --> 00:14:11,683
Sorry I asked.

206
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:28,250
Wow!

207
00:14:28,333 --> 00:14:29,600
So this is LeGru.

208
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:32,120
Ow, that hurt.

209
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:34,097
Then you shouldn't be biting people.

210
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,080
I'll say.

211
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:37,397
Why is everyone ganging up on me?

212
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:40,237
I was trying to break the tension
with a stupid joke is all.

213
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:42,614
Bite me again and I'll cut you in half.

214
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,390
Yes, ma 'am.

215
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:47,820
Oh, look!

216
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,661
Hey, I just remembered something.

217
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:57,657
Right before those salamanders attacked
us, you got a message from your friend.

218
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,480
Oh, I totally forgot.

219
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,098
Rekon's not online.

220
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,459
Maybe he's asleep.

221
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:07,377
Okay, well, why don't you
log out and give him a call?

222
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:09,497
Yeah, I think I better check in with him.

223
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:10,917
I'll only be gone a sec.

224
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,353
Wait for me here, okay?

225
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:16,280
Yui, would you please keep
an eye on my avatar? Me?

226
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:20,557
Yeah, I need to make sure your dad
doesn't mess around with it while I'm out.

227
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:21,699
Copy that, ma 'am.

228
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,155
You gotta be kidding.

229
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,177
I'm sorry.

230
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:52,100
Hey, Nagata.

231
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:53,557
What's with all the calls?

232
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:56,380
What do you want? You picked up! Finally!

233
00:15:56,740 --> 00:15:58,093
Where were you, Suguha?

234
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:01,160
Oh, I was dealing with some in-game stuff.

235
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:04,020
We got trouble, like, like, big trouble.

236
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:06,777
Sigurd's coming after
us, and that's not all.

237
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:09,260
He betrayed Sakuya, the self-commander.

238
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:11,837
Betrayed her? How?

239
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:15,567
Start from the beginning and
tell me everything that happened.

240
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,137
But we're running out of time.

241
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:21,338
Okay, remember when the salamanders
ambushed us in the ancient forest?

242
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:24,440
Didn't that whole setup
seem a little weird to you?

243
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:26,331
I don't know, not really.

244
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:27,877
Why do you think it was weird?

245
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:32,157
Remember how Sigurd said he'd be the decoy
and then he lured three of them away?

246
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,200
Yeah, now that you mention it.

247
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:36,037
Don't you think it was out of character?

248
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:39,179
I mean, usually he'd make
someone else do it, right?

249
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:40,780
Yeah, I guess.

250
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:45,254
I mean, you're right, it's
weird, but what's your point?

251
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:47,760
Okay, here it is.

252
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:51,711
I found out he's been working
as a spy for the Salamanders,

253
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:53,340
probably for a while now.

254
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:54,750
What?

255
00:16:54,833 --> 00:16:57,457
Do you have proof or did
you just hear about it?

256
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:59,697
Remember how I said
something was bugging me?

257
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:04,074
Well, I used a transparency spell and
I've been following Sigurd all day.

258
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:06,937
I tracked him to a back alley,

259
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:10,557
and I saw him and a couple others
put on invisibility cloaks.

260
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:13,169
They were up to something,
that's for sure.

261
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:16,877
I followed them down into the sewers where

262
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:19,548
these two sketchy guys
were waiting for him.

263
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,860
I couldn't believe it.

264
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:23,354
They were salamanders.

265
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:26,957
They were a little ways away from
me, so I couldn't hear everything.

266
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:30,334
But I heard the salamander
say they put a tracer on you.

267
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:42,380
Keep going? Then what?

268
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:44,580
The salamander's caught me.

269
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:48,095
I'm still in the sewers,
paralyzed by the poison arrow.

270
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:51,827
Well, now I know why
you kept calling me IRL.

271
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:54,433
There's something else.

272
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:58,517
Sakuya is supposed to form an
alliance with the Cats today.

273
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:03,157
The meeting's in neutral territory and
she's heading there right now, in secret.

274
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,769
Sigurd knows about it too.

275
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:09,136
He's gonna show up at the signing
ceremony with his guns and attack it!

276
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:14,660
We have to hurry!

277
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,240
Hey, welcome back, Leafa.

278
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,518
Yeah, welcome back.

279
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:21,480
Kirito, I have to leave. Why?

280
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:26,077
Sorry, but there's something I
have to take care of right away.

281
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:28,866
If I had time to explain,
believe me, I would.

282
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:32,786
But I can't, and I don't think
I'll be coming back here either.

283
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:36,457
Then I guess you'll just have
to explain it to me on the way.

284
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:39,357
It'll take a while to get out
of here because we can't fly.

285
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:40,969
That's enough time, right?

286
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,180
Yeah, right.

287
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:54,697
Forty minutes from now, in
the Valley of the Butterflies,

288
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:58,037
the leaders of the Sylphs and the
Cats are gonna have a meeting.

289
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:00,777
Mind if I ask a couple
questions before we get there?

290
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:01,690
Go ahead.

291
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:04,577
If the Salamanders attack
the Sylphs and the Catseas,

292
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,660
what are they gonna get out of it?

293
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:09,777
For one, they'd stop the
Alliance from happening.

294
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:13,477
And if the Cats find out their leader
died because a Sylph turned traitor,

295
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:15,557
they'd be pretty pissed, wouldn't they?

296
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,470
Super pissed.

297
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:20,697
It's a good way to start a war between
the Cats and the Sylphs, that's for sure.

298
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:22,717
It's also a good way to get rich.

299
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:26,677
If you take out the leader of a
territory, you get 30 % of its money.

300
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:31,054
You can invade its hometown for 10
days and charge whatever tax you want.

301
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:33,480
No way. Really? Seriously.

302
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:34,978
Would I lie to you?

303
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:37,242
This isn't your problem, Kirito.

304
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,597
It's a sylph problem.

305
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:42,057
You don't have any reason to get
involved and risk your life over it.

306
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:45,357
If we go to the meeting, chances
are we won't make it back alive.

307
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:48,793
And we'll probably have to
start over from Sylvain again.

308
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:51,460
But this could work for you.

309
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:54,417
You want to get to the
top of the World Tree,

310
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:57,860
so you might be better off
working with the Salamanders.

311
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,660
If they can pull this off,

312
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,737
it'll give them the
power and resources they

313
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:06,037
need to make an attempt at the World Tree.

314
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:09,885
And since you're a Spriggan, they
might hire you as a mercenary.

315
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:13,100
So, if you wanted to kill me, you could.

316
00:20:13,660 --> 00:20:15,484
I wouldn't hold it against you.

317
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:20,997
It's just a game in the end.

318
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,137
Anything goes, right?

319
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:23,985
If you want to kill, you kill.

320
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:26,100
If you want to steal, you steal.

321
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:31,737
A lot of people think like
that, more than I care to know.

322
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:33,880
And in a way, I get it.

323
00:20:34,340 --> 00:20:36,164
Even I used to think like that.

324
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:39,740
But none of it's true.

325
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:45,057
In a virtual world, there's things you have
to protect because it's a virtual world.

326
00:20:45,140 --> 00:20:46,964
Someone special taught me that.

327
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:50,693
If you give in to your impulses in here,

328
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:53,980
it's going to change who
you are in the real world.

329
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:57,521
The player and the character
are one and the same.

330
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:00,360
Leafa, you're a good person.

331
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:03,006
And I want to be your friend.

332
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:05,973
So it doesn't matter what the reason is.

333
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:10,041
There's no way in hell I'd ever
attack a friend for my own benefit.

334
00:21:10,280 --> 00:21:11,927
I couldn't live with myself.

335
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:16,780
Kirito, I...

336
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,380
Thank you.

337
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:27,417
Wow, I sounded pretentious, didn't I?

338
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:29,340
Sorry about that. Uh-oh.

339
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,080
That was pretty cool.

340
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:33,460
Oh, crap.

341
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:35,497
We're wasting time just standing here.

342
00:21:35,580 --> 00:21:37,540
We gotta go. Yui, lead the way.

343
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:39,140
You got it, Daddy.

344
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:40,972
Here, give me your hand.

345
00:21:41,060 --> 00:21:43,160
Okay, but... Come on!

346
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:51,740
Ah! The monsters!

347
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:54,880
Ah!

348
00:21:58,140 --> 00:21:59,320
Here's the exit!

349
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:47,880
but I can't wait to see you again.

350
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:49,819
It's time for now.

351
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:54,957
I don't know if I can't
wait to see you again.

352
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:58,337
I can't wait to see you again.

353
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:03,117
I can't

354
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:08,577
wait to

355
00:23:08,660 --> 00:23:09,800
see you again.

356
00:23:12,480 --> 00:23:16,377
I'll see you

357
00:23:16,460 --> 00:23:19,217
next

358
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:26,300
time,

359
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,066
General of the Blazing Flame.

360
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:40,130
You
